cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite Premia Lab and record the exact commit used; historical scores are development results, not live performance."
title: "Premia Lab: Causal Forecasts and Cost-Aware Portfolios"
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-30"
authors:
  - family-names: Lemonnier
    given-names: Hugo
repository-code: "https://github.com/hlemonnier/premia-lab"
url: "https://github.com/hlemonnier/premia-lab"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A quantitative research workbench for characteristic-factor return estimation,
  conditional risk and transaction-cost-aware portfolio construction. The maintained
  N0 policy combines shared-premium estimates with a bounded own-stock residual
  correction. The project retains causal execution tests, matched controls and
  negative findings. An independent synthetic demo runs without benchmark inputs;
  recorded historical scores concern an exposed simulated development sample.
keywords:
  - quantitative finance
  - quantitative research
  - factor models
  - portfolio optimization
  - risk management
  - transaction costs
  - backtesting
  - time series
  - statistical learning
  - reproducible research
  - synthetic data
  - Python
